{
  "out": "/tmp/photonz-playtest/effects-remembered",
  "seed": "Everything you do to a shape's effects should stick for the next shape of that kind. Reported by the user on 2026-09-07: a rectangle arrived with a blur, they took the blur off, drew another, and the blur was back. Adding reached the tool and removing did not. This walk draws a fresh shape after every move (add, remove, switch off, reorder) and holds the new shape to what the last one was left wearing. It also draws ellipses in the middle, which must keep their own effects and never take a rectangle's. Since 2026-09-08 a shape arrives holding a Border, so a list with nothing added to it holds that one row and no other, and the walk names the effect it is asking about rather than counting crosses. An arrived Border is the one effect that is not kept as a row when you switch it off: the next box comes out with no ring AND no Border row, so the walk puts one back from the plus, and what comes back is a plain new border rather than the Inside one the last box was told to draw.",
  "setup": { "forget": ["panel", "shapes", "tools"] },
  "steps": [
