      "note": "the border was switched off rather than removed. The next box comes out with no ring and no Border row at all, because an arrived Border switched off is remembered as no border rather than as a border that is off, and the Inside it was told to sit at goes with the row. The plus puts a plain new border back, Outside, which is what a border added from the plus always is. Whether switching off should instead keep the row, off, with its width and position on it, is the open question in the task Switching a shape border off loses the row on the next shape." },
